  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nInstallation of `matrix-synapse` as outlined [here](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/docs/workers.md#setting-up-workers) using `pip install matrix-synapse[all]` or `pip install matrix-synapse[redis]` does not work. Pip claims `pip: No match.`\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nInstall `matrix-synapse` from source and execute `pip install matrix-synapse[all]` or `pip install matrix-synapse[redis]`.\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\n\r\nInstall dependencies manually (in this case redis dependencies):\r\n\r\n```\r\npip install txredisapi hiredis\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n| Software | Version |\r\n| :------------: | ----------: |\r\n| matrix-synapse | 1.25.0 |\r\n| python | 3.9.1 |\r\n| redis | 6.0.10 |\r\n\r\n### Platform\r\n\r\n**OS** in use is **FreeBSD 12.2-RELEASE-p1 GENERIC amd64**",
